WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.025
Coding Exercise 6 combines row filtering grouping
aggregation and a group threshold

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:10.425
using the grades table The requirement is
specifically for Fall 2024 so

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:15.425
semester equals Fall 2024 is a row-level condition
Put that in WHERE

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.838
so only rows from the requested semester enter the
groups The grain

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:23.862
is one row per course so GROUP BY course For each
course

00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:28.912
calculate the average grade and enrollment AVG grade
gives the mean score

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.812
and COUNT star gives the number of student grade
rows in the

00:00:31.825 --> 00:00:37.488
group Give both expressions clear aliases The report
should include only

00:00:37.512 --> 00:00:41.850
courses with at least fifty students That condition
depends on the group

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:45.188
count so write HAVING COUNT star greater than or
equal to fifty

00:00:46.075 --> 00:00:50.788
Finally sort the courses with the highest average
first Run and Check

00:00:50.975 --> 00:00:55.988
then inspect whether every returned course meets the
enrollment threshold This exercise

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.562
is useful because it combines the entire aggregation
workflow row population grain

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.188
measures group filter and analytical sort
